# Repo-root .dockerignore.
#
# This is the one that actually matters for `docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile .`
# run from the repo root: Docker resolves .dockerignore relative to the build
# CONTEXT directory, not the Dockerfile's directory. Since the context for that
# command is the repo root (the trailing "."), apps/api/.dockerignore is never
# read — only this file is. Without it, the Dockerfile's `COPY apps/api ./apps/api`
# and `COPY packages/shared ./packages/shared` would copy real .env files
# (containing secrets) and node_modules straight into the build-stage image layer.
.git
**/.env
**/node_modules
**/dist
.worktrees
